// Source: Source: Wier, The Childs Own Music Book (1918), p.49. https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Page:Childs_own_music_book.djvu/57
// Expanded instrumental arrangement. The established melody keeps all pitches, onsets, written durations, rests, tempo and meter. Original plucked/keyboard accompaniment remains; independent low strings sustain its bass line and violin/viola voice its explicitly simultaneous harmonies. Common chord tones are tied, not reattacked. Characteristic light-march percussion marks phrase/rhythmic structure. No choir is used. Standard GM/CC7=100; lead and accompaniment velocities balanced for the larger ensemble.
// Musicbox title: Yankee%20Doodle
